<title>GERMANY: Rheinhyp plans 96 bonus dividend.</title>
<headline>Rheinhyp plans 96 bonus dividend.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>German mortgage bank Rheinische Hypothekenbank AG, a unit of Commerzbank AG, said on Monday it planned to pay an unchanged 1996 dividend of 17 marks plus an anniversary bonus of 2.50 marks per share.</p>
<p>In a mandatory statement, Rheinhyp also said it would pay a special dividend of 35.50 marks per 50-mark par-value share.</p>
<p>The special payout should be reinvested into the bank in accordance with its plans for a capital increase, which are to be proposed at its annual shareholders' meeting on May 7.</p>
<p>The payouts are also subject to supervisory board approval, Rheinhyp said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
